! Rules in rulebook: After (B23_after)
! ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Rule 1/151 ! After going from a room ( called R1 ) to a room ( called R2 ) ( this is the print transition rule ):
! --- now the mid-placed rules ---
! Rule 2/151 ! After margaret going to somewhere ( called the destination ) when the destination is the location ( this is the speak to margaret when she enters the front office rule ):
!   >>> I - Number of aspects constrained >>>
! Rule 3/151 ! After going from somewhere ( called S ) to somewhere ( called T ) when the location is in ELR:
!   >>> III.2.2 - Action/Where/Room Where Action Takes Place >>>
! Rule 4/151 ! After going from the large grave when the wooden frame is nowhere and the player encloses the dowsing rod:
!   >>> III.2.2 - Action/Where/Room Where Action Takes Place >>>
! Rule 5/151 ! After going to the Horton Family House Parlor for the first time:
!   >>> III.5.1 - Action/When/Duration >>>
! Rule 6/151 ! After going to the large grave when the wooden frame is nowhere and the player encloses the dowsing rod:
!   >>> III.5.2 - Action/When/Circumstances >>>
! Rule 7/151 ! After going to Solvay-Road-by-the-lake when the player encloses the Mystic Compass:
!   === equally specific with ===
! Rule 8/151 ! After going to Enigma Lake Town Hall when the player encloses the Mystic Compass:
!   >>> III.2.2 - Action/Where/Room Where Action Takes Place >>>
! Rule 9/151 ! After Margaret going to a room:
!   >>> III.2.2 - Action/Where/Room Where Action Takes Place >>>
! Rule 10/151 ! After giving Tribes of New York to Doris when Tribes of New York is not delivered and about the mission is exhausted:
!   === equally specific with ===
! Rule 11/151 ! After giving the cup of coffee to Christy when Christy carries Tribes of New York and Christy is not researching:
!   >>> III.3.2 - Action/What/Thing Acted On >>>
! Rule 12/151 ! After giving a loanable tome to Minerva when the borrowed book-minerva is the noun:
!   === equally specific with ===
! Rule 13/151 ! After putting a loanable tome on the mahogany desk when the borrowed book-minerva is the noun:
!   === equally specific with ===
