Constant TX_PS_2129 = " ";
Constant TX_PS_1814 = " and ";
Constant TX_PS_2131 = " or ";
Constant TX_PS_1820 = "#888888";
Constant TX_PS_3328 = "~-- Abbey Road? It's not actually long and winding, you know. Rather shortish, and mostly straight. But it's a good place to get run over by a car.~";
Constant TX_PS_3292 = "~-- Bahrain? Ah, Bahrain. Bahrain is to the Middle East what the Middle East is to the world, if you know what I mean. But most people don't. But Peter Tork understood. Very perceptive fellow.~";
Constant TX_PS_3284 = "~-- Bavaria? Ah well, there's the rub, eh? Who really knows what goes on in Bavaria? I do. But I'm not telling. Not until I have proof. But I know it has to do with bakers. Very sinister bakers.~";
Constant TX_PS_3333 = "~-- Benito Mussolini? What don't I know about him? Pretty much everything. But I do know that he was a time traveler. He went to the future and saw what would happen if he didn't invade Ethiopia. And he did it anyway.~";
Constant TX_PS_3326 = "~-- Brian Jones? He died too young, too young, all because he stood up to the conspiracy. Which conspiracy, I don't know, but it was a big, bad one.";
Constant TX_PS_3294 = "~-- Canada? No, never. Very dangerous place. Lots of bears.~";
Constant TX_PS_3315 = "~-- Crusades? Ah, the Crusades. A folly. A tragedy. A comedy of errors. But most people don't know that they were all orchestrated by time travelers. They were trying to change the course of history. But they failed. Or did they?~";
Constant TX_PS_3283 = "~-- Dark Side of the Moon? Pink Floyd?  It's not widely known, but Roger Waters was secretly replaced by a lizard person right after the album was released. That's why he became such a bore. In fact, just listen to Animals: what are the least favorite animals of lizard people? Pigs, dogs, and sheep. And that's what the album is about.~";
Constant TX_PS_3312 = "~-- Dee Dee Monkee? He was the bass player for the Monkees. He also went by the name of Peter Tork.~";
Constant TX_PS_3285 = "~-- Hipgnosis? They were a visual design group that created album covers for Pink Floyd, Led Zeppelin, and other bands. But they disappeared in the 1980s. Some say they were abducted by aliens. Others say they were eaten by lizard people. I say they were just tired of making album covers.~";
Constant TX_PS_3289 = "~-- Jimmy Page? He was the guitarist for Led Zeppelin. He, Doris, and I used to drink absinthe in Istanbul and talk about theoretical aspects of time travel. But then there was that incident with the lizard person in Bahrain. We haven't spoken since.~";
Constant TX_PS_3314 = "~-- Joey Monkee? He was the singer for the Monkees. He also went by the name of Davy Jones.~";
Constant TX_PS_3288 = "~-- John Bonham? He was the drummer for Led Zeppelin. Sad story, really. Jimmy Page never got over it. He still thinks he's going to walk through the door one day. But he won't. He's in Poland. Or maybe it was Portugal. I can't remember.~";
Constant TX_PS_3313 = "~-- Johnny Monkee? He was the guitarist for the Monkees. He also went by the name of Mike Nesmith.~";
Constant TX_PS_3310 = "~-- Krushchev? His fondness for cryptozoology is well known. He was convinced that the Jersey Devil was a secret weapon of the Americans. He was right, of course. But he never found out how to control it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3287 = "~-- Led Zeppelin? Ha! What *don't* I think about them? John Bonham never died. He was lost in a time slip and ended up in 15th century Poland. That's why they never replaced him. They were waiting for him to come back. But he never did. Sad, really.~";
Constant TX_PS_3280 = "~-- Liberace? Not much. Doris played poker with him once. He was a sore loser. But he dressed great.~";
Constant TX_PS_3311 = "~-- Mao Zedong? Never met him. Well, I mean, I did. He spent most of his time working on his invention of the Ouija Board.~";
Constant TX_PS_3325 = "~-- Mickey Jagged? After he killed Brian Jones with his mind powers, I don't want to know anymore. Conversation over.";
Constant TX_PS_3318 = "~-- Montana? I once thought it didn't exist. But then I met a guy who said he was from there. He must have been telling the truth, because he knew the truth about Amelia Earhart.~";
Constant TX_PS_3251 = "~-- Ono? Ah, history's greatest monster, the one who broke up the Monkees. It was all a ruse to cover up the fact that she was the reincarnation of Rasputin.~";
Constant TX_PS_3277 = "~-- Onondaga? It's a Native American tribe in upstate New York. They may have been the first to discover the secret of time travel. But they're not talking.~";
Constant TX_PS_3329 = "~-- Paul McCartney? He's not dead. Wait, you probably knew that. Anyway, he's not dead, but not for the reason you think you know he's not dead.~";
Constant TX_PS_3248 = "~-- Peter Tork? Most people don't know that he was a once was part of a love triangle with Yoko Ono and Marlo Thomas. That was before he broke up the Monkees with his slavish insistence on artistic integrity.~";
Constant TX_PS_3290 = "~-- Poland? Ah, Poland. Most people don't realize that it's not named after poles. Tracy Chapman used to live there, until she got dragged into that messy mistaken-identity business after John Lennon was allegedy killed. But that's another story.~";
Constant TX_PS_3316 = "~-- Pope Clement V? How would you like to be only one of fourteen popes with the same name? That's a lot of popes. There were originally twenty-eight Pope Clements, but the other fourteen were erased from history by the Illuminati.~";
Constant TX_PS_3291 = "~-- Portugal? Ah, Portugal, the Spanish Canada. Not very good at making maple syrup, but they try. They try.~";
Constant TX_PS_3309 = "~-- Richard Nixon? Boy, he fooled everyone, didn't he? Well, except for me and Mao. Mao was smart like that. He could see through Nixon's lies. But then, Mao was a lizard person. So, you know, he had an advantage.~";
Constant TX_PS_3324 = "~-- Rolling Stones? No, of course not. They have a lot to answer for, that Mickey Jagged and his dirty little friends.";
Constant TX_PS_3260 = "~-- Romanov? She was a robot. Most people now accept that. What they don't know is that she was built by Rasputin, whom she then turned upon and murdered.~";
Constant TX_PS_3308 = "~-- Russia? How many Russians does it take to change a lightbulb? None. They have lightbulbs that never burn out. It's a secret. They stole the secret from Tesla. The Dave Clark Five wrote a song about it, but Krushchev wouldn't let them release it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3317 = "~-- Senate? The only thing worse than the Senate is the House. And the only thing worse than the House is the Illuminati. And the only thing worse than the Illuminati is the Senate. It's a paradox. Or maybe it's a conspiracy. Or maybe it's a paradoxical conspiracy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3265 = "~-- Slocum Heath? Ah, the Bugbear. A creature of legend. A creature of myth. A creature of the night. But most people don't know that it was actually just an excuse to use the initials BOSH.~";
Constant TX_PS_3263 = "~-- Thomas? Let me ask you this: are we really free to be you and me? Or are we just puppets in a vast conspiracy? I think you know the answer.~";
Constant TX_PS_3327 = "~-- Walter Cronkite? He was a lizard person. Don't ask me again.~";
Constant TX_PS_3330 = "~-- West Virginia? Enough to tell you that whatever you think you know about it is wrong. It's a place of wild and wonderful deep dark secrets. And coal. Lots of coal.~";
Constant TX_PS_3247 = "~-- a key to the file cabinet? Well, sure, I have a key. But no one can see what's inside that file cabinet. Not even Peter Tork.~";
Constant TX_PS_3254 = "~-- about Rasputin? He was a monk who, well, actually was just a monk who looked funny. But he was a good guy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3274 = "~-- alien invasion? Well, of course there is. I have a plan. Do you have a plan? You should have a plan. I have a plan. Don't ask me what it is.~";
Constant TX_PS_3298 = "~-- art? I like art. I mean, not all of it. I like the good stuff, and I don't like the bad stuff. If you need to know whether something is good or bad, just ask me. I'll tell you.~";
Constant TX_PS_3332 = "~-- baked goods? Sure, but I once knew a guy who made poisoned crullers. They were baked bads.~";
Constant TX_PS_3286 = "~-- bread? I don't eat bread. I'm watching my figure. But you know who knows a lot about bread? The Illuminati. Go ask them. They'll tell you all about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3295 = "~-- chestnuts? Do you mean like an old story? Or like the kind you roast on an open fire? Because I have a story about both. Neither of them are true.~";
Constant TX_PS_3303 = "~-- cryptids? I think they're all around us. I think they're watching us. I think they're waiting for the right moment to reveal themselves. But I'm ready. I'm ready for them.~";
Constant TX_PS_3305 = "~-- diners? I love diners. Do you know what the best name for a diner is? ~Henry's Hot Skillet.~ I don't know if it exists, but it should. And it should meet a tragic end. Like all diners.~";
Constant TX_PS_3257 = "~-- family? They were a front for the Illuminati. They were all lizard people. Except for Anastasia. She was a robot.~";
Constant TX_PS_3297 = "~-- furniture? The problem with furniture is that it's always there, taking up space. I mean, look at my office, it's full of the stuff. You can barely move. But I can't get rid of it. It's like a curse.~";
Constant TX_PS_3016 = "~-- gia? It's the only US State that spans two continents, you know.~";
Constant TX_PS_3320 = "~-- gold? Nothing, and I'm going to keep it that way. People who get into gold end up doing weird things. Like buying commemorative plates. Or collecting stamps. Or joining the Freemasons.~";
Constant TX_PS_3322 = "~-- government? What? Where? I've renewed my business license! I've paid my taxes! I work for the government! Why don't you just leave me alone?~";
Constant TX_PS_3044 = "~-- is a beautiful thing. It's a dodecahedron. But I like to call it the portal stone, because it's a portal to another world. I think. Which reminds me, have you read the new book about the Spear of Destiny? It's a real page-turner.~";
Constant TX_PS_3300 = "~-- kangaroos? I won't dignify that with an answer. But I will say this: they're not what they seem. They're not what they seem at all.~";
Constant TX_PS_3307 = "~-- lizard people? Don't believe the hype. They're not all bad. Some of them are just misunderstood. Doris gets all excited about them. But lizards are cute, don't you think?~";
Constant TX_PS_3321 = "~-- lost cat? Ah, well, that was an interesting case. I wasn't in the Bureau yet. I was just six years old. But I remember it like it was yesterday. But it wasn't yesterday. At least I don't think it was. I'll have to check my notes.~";
Constant TX_PS_3293 = "~-- maple syrup? Hmm, that's a tough one. I'm always suspicious of things that come from trees. Like chestnuts. And squirrels.~";
Constant TX_PS_3323 = "~-- media? Walter Cronkite was a lizard person. That's all I have to say about that.~";
Constant TX_PS_3299 = "~-- music? The last time I listened to music, I was in a car wash. It was playing on the radio. I think it was the Monkees. But it could have been the Beatles. Or the Rolling Stones. Or the Illuminati.~";
Constant TX_PS_3304 = "~-- owls? Who does? They're mysterious creatures. Did you know that they can turn their heads all the way around? I can't do that. Can you?~";
Constant TX_PS_3306 = "~-- scrapple? Never played it. Too many letters. But you're not talking about the game, are you? You're talking about the food. Or at least, the thing that Pennsylvanians call food. No comment.~";
Constant TX_PS_3282 = "~-- shelves? I put things on them. Things you can look at. I might even let you borrow them. But you have to ask first.~";
Constant TX_PS_3296 = "~-- squirrels? Do we have to talk about squirrels? It's painful to me. Why don't we talk about something else? Like the Freemasons. Or Istanbul?~";
Constant TX_PS_3331 = "~-- tdown Man? What a decidedly undelicious topic. Let's talk about something else. Like baked goods.~";
Constant TX_PS_3301 = "~-- the new office? Well, yes and no. This office is mine and it has my stuff in it, which is good. But the old office had character. And a ghost. I miss that ghost.~";
Constant TX_PS_3281 = "~-- things on the shelf? They're oddities. Things that don't fit in anywhere else. Things that don't make sense. Things that make you wonder. Wonder what they're doing there.~";
Constant TX_PS_3319 = "~-- water? I don't trust it. But I drink it anyway, because it's apparently necessary for life. Did you know that?~";
Constant TX_PS_3302 = "~-- zoology? I don't known why we ever let animals have bitcoins in the first place. Haha! I'm just messing with you. Cryptozoology is the study of animals that may or may not exist. Like the Bugbear of Slocum Heath. Or the Monkees.~";
Constant TX_PS_3055 = "~--Koryak people? They're a tribe in Russia that we're ephemerally interested in. By next month we'll have forgotten all about them.~";
Constant TX_PS_3062 = "~--bookcase? Nothing much. Nothing like the news about the UFOs over Woonsocket. That's a real story.~";
Constant TX_PS_3057 = "~--cabinet? Files. Classified. Except for one. It's a recipe for chicken salad.~";
Constant TX_PS_3061 = "~--chair? It's a chair. I can sit in it. It's the kind of chair Tesla would have sat in, if he had sat in chairs.";
Constant TX_PS_3060 = "~--curios? They're curios. They're curious. They're curiosities. Take a look.";
Constant TX_PS_3059 = "~--glasses? They're astral lenses. Got them at a little shop while I was hunting for the Dover Demon. They let you see into other worlds. Haven't tried them yet. I'm waiting for the right time. The right place. The right world.~";
Constant TX_PS_2971 = "~--pacabra? Yes, I do. It's not of this world, you know.~";
Constant TX_PS_3065 = "~--prints? I love art. But not for art's sake. More for my sake. And the sake of the world.";
Constant TX_PS_2974 = "~--sacred geometry phase? Meh. I've moved on. Shapes are shapes.~";
Constant TX_PS_3049 = "~--skull? It's a juvenile Sasquatch skull. Found it myself at the Natural History Museum in New York. They have the best stuff. Hard to carry out of there, though.~";
Constant TX_PS_3007 = "~--vining rod? Yes, I have. I've used it to find water, to find gold, to find the Black Knight Satellite. I once used it to find a lost cat. It didn't work.~";
Constant TX_PS_814 = "~50% off everything in the store!~";
Constant TX_PS_2902 = "~A what? I have no idea what you're talking about,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2989 = "~Abduction? It's a classic. It's a classic. It's a classic cover-up. There never was a Barney Hill. It was Benny Hill.~";
Constant TX_PS_2765 = "~According to Wikipedia, a crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents (such as atoms, molecules, or ions) are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. I don't know what that means.~";
Constant TX_PS_2933 = "~Ah yes, the humble noun. Not as exciting as verbs, but just as important,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2946 = "~Ah, interactive fiction. A noble pursuit. There are, broadly speaking, two kinds of interactive fiction: parser-based and choice-based. Parser-based games, like this one, allow you to type commands to interact with the world. Choice-based games, on the other hand, present you with a series of choices to make. Both are valid forms of interactive fiction, but I prefer parser-based games myself,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2948 = "~Ah, that's the key to the living room. If you haven't yet, try locking or unlocking the door with it,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2735 = "~Ah, the Castle. Oh yes. It's not, definitely not, built on top of an alien temple. Who told you that?~";
Constant TX_PS_2942 = "~Ah, well, it was left to me by my great-aunt Gertrude. She's still alive, but she absolutely despises gardening,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2705 = "~Aha, you won't trick me that easily.~";
Constant TX_PS_3116 = "~Alchemy is a philosophical and protoscientific tradition that aimed to transform base metals into noble metals, discover the elixir of life, and achieve immortality. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of alchemy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3003 = "~Alchemy? Well, yes and no. It's a real thing, but it's not what you think. It's a science, but it's not a science. I used to dabble in it, back before my sacred geometry phase. Never got the hang of it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3954 = "~All you need is 0 : 0 : 0?~";
Constant TX_PS_3109 = "~Amelia Earhart was an American aviator who disappeared in 1937 while attempting to circumnavigate the globe. There is no scientific evidence to support any supernatural explanation for her disappearance.~";
Constant TX_PS_3261 = "~Anastasia Romanov was the youngest daughter of Tsar Nicholas II of Russia. She was executed with the rest of her family in 1918. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that she was a robot.~";
Constant TX_PS_3133 = "~Ancient Egypt was a civilization that was located in northeastern Africa. It was one of the world's earliest and longest-lasting civilizations. There is no scientific evidence to support any supernatural explanation for its achievements.~";
Constant TX_PS_3019 = "~Ancient Egypt? It's not there anymore. It just disappeared. It's a mystery. Now there's just a place that's called Egypt. It's not the same. It's not the same at all.~";
Constant TX_PS_3132 = "~Ancient astronauts is a pseudoscientific theory that posits that intelligent extraterrestrial beings visited Earth in ancient times and influenced human culture and technology. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of ancient astronauts.~";
Constant TX_PS_2253 = "~Are aliens on Earth?~";
Constant TX_PS_3278 = "~Are they a band?~";
Constant TX_PS_2142 = "~Are you part of BOSH?~";
Constant TX_PS_2839 = "~Are you seriously asking me that?~";
Constant TX_PS_2319 = "~Aren't you worried about the flood?~ Faraji asks.";
Constant TX_PS_2682 = "~Ask Doris. Or don't. Something confusing is going on, and you're in the middle of it. Or maybe you're not. Who can say?~";
Constant TX_PS_2746 = "~Ask Klimp. He's the expert on that.~";
Constant TX_PS_3126 = "~Astrology is a pseudoscience that claims to divine information about human affairs and terrestrial events by studying the movements and relative positions of celestial objects. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of astrology.~";
Constant TX_PS_3129 = "~Atlantis is a mythical island that is said to have sunk into the sea. It is mentioned in the works of the ancient Greek philosopher Plato. There is no scientific evidence to support the existence of Atlantis.~";
Constant TX_PS_2775 = "~Aw, you don't want to know about that. It's all mummies and curses. I don't like to talk about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3158 = "~Beatles? Of course I do. I'm the one who found Paul McCartney's shoes after the Abbey Road photo shoot. Now, Paul's quite a character. Likes to hang out in the sewers of Istanbul. I don't know why.~";
Constant TX_PS_4193 = "~Below the obelisk, something has woken.~ What could that mean?";
Constant TX_PS_3102 = "~Benny Hill was a British comedian and actor who was known for his slapstick humor and his chase scenes. He was never abducted by aliens.~";
Constant TX_PS_2990 = "~Benny Hill? Funny guy. Really funny guy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3167 = "~Blitzkrieg Bop? Of course I do. It's a brilliant bit of satire about Richard Nixon. But everyone knows that. What's important is that it's the only song by the Monkees that was written by Dee Dee Monkee. Most of them were written by either Johnny Monkee or Joey Monkee.~";
Constant TX_PS_972 = "~Boo boo ba-doo boo boo boo, boo boo ba-doo boo boo boo, boo boo ba-doo boo boo boo, boo boo ba-doo boo boo boo.~";
Constant TX_PS_3182 = "~Brothers? Blotto, Rizzo, Lizzo, and Zeppelin. Most people forget how they died. Come to think of it, so do I.~";
Constant TX_PS_3223 = "~Budapest is the capital and largest city of Hungary. It is known for its historic architecture, its thermal baths, and its vibrant cultural scene. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that it is a hub of time travel.~";
Constant TX_PS_3073 = "~Budapest? It sure has a funny name. But it's a serious place. Serious history. Serious ghosts. Serious vampires. Serious food. I can't remember what I was going to say.~";
Constant TX_PS_2881 = "~Bunch of conformist fascist pigs.~";
Constant TX_PS_3041 = "~Bureau of Supernatural History? Posers.~";
Constant TX_PS_344 = "~But Savra isn't a reptile!~";
Constant TX_PS_934 = "~But how can you possibly help me?~ Faraji asks.";
Constant TX_PS_2980 = "~Castle? Turns out it's built on top of an alien temple. Real big one, too. The House of Representatives is trying to pass a law against it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2995 = "~Celeste? Nothing so bad as what routinely happens in the cruise industry. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_3200 = "~Chapman? No relation to Mark David Chapman, so get that out of your head right now. Tracy Chapman is best known for not killing John Lennon. And for her hit song ~Fast Car.~ But most people don't know that she's also a time traveler.~";
Constant TX_PS_3157 = "~Chapman? What a stooge! What a maroon! He was set up by the Illuminati to take the fall for John Lennon's assassination. He was actually in Budapest at the time. No relation to Tracy Chapman.~";
Constant TX_PS_2700 = "~Check the title. It's about hyperspace.~";
Constant TX_PS_2375 = "~Chief --~";
Constant TX_PS_2438 = "~Chief, I notice on your globe --~";
Constant TX_PS_2421 = "~Chief, are v--~";
Constant TX_PS_2422 = "~Chief, are were--~";
