Constant TX_PS_2666 = "~Chief, what's your take on crypto--~";
Constant TX_PS_2446 = "~Chief, where is --~";
Constant TX_PS_2412 = "~Chief, who are the Free--~";
Constant TX_PS_2372 = "~Chief, who is D--";
Constant TX_PS_2453 = "~Chief, why do you talk about --~";
Constant TX_PS_2402 = "~Chief, you ever see Raiders of the Lost --~";
Constant TX_PS_2408 = "~Chief, you ever use --~";
Constant TX_PS_2436 = "~Chief, you have such a nice office --~";
Constant TX_PS_2543 = "~Chief, you like the --~";
Constant TX_PS_2406 = "~Chief, you mentioned --~";
Constant TX_PS_2400 = "~Chief,~ Faraji asks, ~is the Holy --~";
Constant TX_PS_2707 = "~Christy is our researcher. They also have a good eye for color. They helped me pick out the paint for my kitchen.~";
Constant TX_PS_2690 = "~Christy is the field office researcher. Cynical little sweetheart, you'd think they'd be more cheerful with all that color in their office.~";
Constant TX_PS_2676 = "~Christy is the field office researcher. They're very good at what they do, if the way they do it is what you need. You can find them in their office, west and then south.~";
Constant TX_PS_3172 = "~Clark Five? I refuse to answer that question on the grounds that it might incriminate me.~";
Constant TX_PS_2685 = "~Coffee is strange. It smells good, but it tastes horrible.~";
Constant TX_PS_3097 = "~Colonel Sanders was the founder of Kentucky Fried Chicken. His name was definitely Harland David Sanders.~";
Constant TX_PS_2985 = "~Colonel Sanders? No one even knows his real name. He's a mystery wrapped in a secret recipe.~";
Constant TX_PS_2927 = "~Commands are the lifeblood of interactive fiction. You can't do much without them. I wrote a book on the subject, you know. It's in the room south of here. My favorite command? GIVE DOCTOR FLOWER,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2986 = "~Confederacy? No one even knows if it even existed. I mean, you ever meet anyone from the Confederacy? I haven't.~";
Constant TX_PS_3134 = "~Crop circles are patterns that are created by flattening crops, such as wheat or barley, in fields. They are often attributed to extraterrestrial activity or paranormal phenomena. There is no scientific evidence to support these claims.~";
Constant TX_PS_3122 = "~Crystals are solid materials that are formed by the repeating pattern of atoms or molecules. They are used in jewelry, technology, and alternative medicine. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of crystal healing.~";
Constant TX_PS_2863 = "~Cures everything, they say.~";
Constant TX_PS_2915 = "~Daniels will take us to the Dragon, or he will die,~ hisses the lizard person.";
Constant TX_PS_2904 = "~Daniels? Who's Daniels?~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_3219 = "~Davy Jones was a British singer, songwriter, and actor who was best known as a member of the Monkees. He was also a successful solo artist. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he was a vampire.~";
Constant TX_PS_2715 = "~Definitely not a secret window into my soul. Just some things I like.~";
Constant TX_PS_2979 = "~Demon? It's no demon. It's a monkey crossed with a snowy owl. By the way, have you seen the news about the recently discovered alien temple under the basement of the Smithsonian Castle?~";
Constant TX_PS_3197 = "~Depression? Some people say it was caused by the stock market crash of 1929. But I know the truth. A truth I cannot bring myself to utter. But it rhymes with ~lizard people.~";
Constant TX_PS_2275 = "~Did you ever see the Piltdown Man?~";
Constant TX_PS_2266 = "~Did you know Harry S Truman?~";
Constant TX_PS_2269 = "~Did you live through the Great Depression?~";
Constant TX_PS_2268 = "~Did you see any action in World War II?~";
Constant TX_PS_3121 = "~Divining is a practice that is said to allow people to locate water, minerals, and other hidden objects using a divining rod or other tools. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of divining.~";
Constant TX_PS_2258 = "~Do you have any opinions about the Monkees?~";
Constant TX_PS_2273 = "~Do you know Neil Patrick Harris?~";
Constant TX_PS_2667 = "~Do you know anything about --~";
Constant TX_PS_2169 = "~Do you know what this compass is?~";
Constant TX_PS_2309 = "~Do you know where I could get a few bucks?~";
Constant TX_PS_2147 = "~Do you like coffee?~";
Constant TX_PS_2404 = "~Do you really think the Illuminati are in the --~";
Constant TX_PS_2425 = "~Do you think anyone will ever --~";
Constant TX_PS_1339 = "~Doctor, may I borrow your book?~";
Constant TX_PS_2733 = "~Does it really matter? It's not in Enigma Lake.~";
Constant TX_PS_2786 = "~Doesn't exist, although if it did it would explain a lot of things that have happened to me.~";
Constant TX_PS_2877 = "~Don't tell anyone, but I LARP as a vampire on weekends.~";
Constant TX_PS_2762 = "~Don't worry about it. It's not going to happen. I've got a plan.~";
Constant TX_PS_3204 = "~Doogie Howser, M.D. was an American television series that aired from 1989 to 1993. It starred Neil Patrick Harris as a teenage doctor. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he was played by Mark David Chapman.~";
Constant TX_PS_3074 = "~Doris in Pompeii? You'll never know. The evidence was conveniently destroyed somehow.";
Constant TX_PS_2909 = "~Doris is a fool,~ hisses the lizard person. ~He will not stop us.~";
Constant TX_PS_2834 = "~Doris is the chief of the hyperspatial field office. I have no problem with his leadership. No, I certainly wouldn't ever say that.~";
Constant TX_PS_2675 = "~Doris is the field office chief,~ Maggie says dreamily. ~He's a riddle, wrapped in bacon, inside an egg. You can find him in his office, west of here.~";
Constant TX_PS_1130 = "~Doris must have given you a recall button. I can rejigger it to send me to the hyperspace office and send you back to Swamp Park. Alright, give me the button.~";
Constant TX_PS_2329 = "~Doris sent me,~ says Faraji.";
Constant TX_PS_2967 = "~Doris? He's a friend of mine. Works for the Bureau. Sort of. Snappy dresser. Prone to outlandish stories. Ask him about the Mothman.~";
Constant TX_PS_3079 = "~Doris? I don't know any Doris. Who's Doris?~";
Constant TX_PS_2842 = "~Drawings. Of things. I'm not going to show you.~";
Constant TX_PS_3235 = "~Dwight D. Eisenhower was the 34th President of the United States. He served from 1953 to 1961 and was a five-star general in the United States Army during World War II. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he lived in a shack in Enigma Lake.~";
Constant TX_PS_3135 = "~ESP, or extrasensory perception, is the ability to perceive information by means other than the known senses. It is considered a pseudoscience by the scientific community. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of ESP.~";
Constant TX_PS_3021 = "~ESP? Is that like ESPN? I like ESPN. Don't really like sports, but I like ESPN. I like people discussing irrelevant things with passion. Like Senator Savra. He's like ESPN, thinks everything's a game. But I don't think that's what you meant.~";
Constant TX_PS_3136 = "~ESPN is a cable sports channel that is owned by the Walt Disney Company. It is known for its coverage of sports events and its sports news programs. Sometimes Klimp listens to it very loudly in his office.~";
Constant TX_PS_3022 = "~ESPN? Yes, I do. It's an Illuminati-free zone. Very refreshing.~";
Constant TX_PS_2872 = "~Ear Pods. Quality sounds. Eighty-five bucks.~";
Constant TX_PS_2997 = "~Earhart? She was murdered by the Freemasons before she even took off. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_3234 = "~Eisenhower? It's not well known, but for a while he abandoned the White House to live in a shack in the town of Enigma Lake, New York. He was trying to get away from the lizard people. Which is foolish, because everyone knows that Enigma Lake is a lizard people stronghold.~";
Constant TX_PS_2992 = "~Event? I have a theory. Most people think Lenin was born on Earth in 1870, but I have evidence that he was born on the Black Knight Satellite and came to Earth in a meteorite that landed in Tunguska in 1908.~";
Constant TX_PS_2777 = "~Extra Sharp Pencil. It's a brand of pencil. I don't know why you're asking me about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_332 = "~Fantastic! Hand it here.~";
Constant TX_PS_2815 = "~First off, I was the one who suggested he use his middle name. And they said I was crazy. Look at him now.~";
Constant TX_PS_2764 = "~First, get a stick. Then teach it to find water. It's a very simple process.~";
Constant TX_PS_2987 = "~Forest Incident? No one knows what really happened. Except me. I know. It's a long story, but it involves a time slip and a bear from another world.~";
Constant TX_PS_3186 = "~Franklin Delano Roosevelt was the 32nd President of the United States. He served from 1933 to 1945 and led the country through the Great Depression and World War II. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he was a superhero.~";
Constant TX_PS_2802 = "~Funny story. I once ran into Davy Jones hanging out with Klimp in Budapest of all places. Klimp denies it to this day.~";
Constant TX_PS_2976 = "~Geez, West Virginia has the lamest cryptids. The Mothman is just a big owl. A big owl from another world.~";
Constant TX_PS_3130 = "~Georgia is a state in the southeastern United States. It is known for its peaches, peanuts, and pecans. It is also known for the Georgia Guidestones. There is no scientific evidence to support any supernatural explanation for them.~";
Constant TX_PS_3137 = "~Ghosts are the spirits of dead people that are said to haunt the living. They are a popular subject in folklore, literature, and popular culture. There is no scientific evidence to support the existence of ghosts.~";
Constant TX_PS_3023 = "~Ghosts? Yes. Ghosts, poltergeists, phantoms, specters, wraiths, apparitions, spooks, spirits, shades, and the undead are all real. I've seen them. I've talked to them. I've been one. I think. I can't remember.~";
Constant TX_PS_314 = "~Go ask Maggie; she can help you.~";
Constant TX_PS_1108 = "~Good old Doris,~ Daniels says. ~Always the man with the plan.~";
Constant TX_PS_3047 = "~Got it from a store run by a guy who might be a vampire. Lots of vampires in the furniture business. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_583 = "~Got one to buy, not one to borrow.~";
Constant TX_PS_318 = "~Great! Be sure to say hi for me.~";
Constant TX_PS_3255 = "~Grigori Rasputin was a Russian mystic and self-proclaimed holy man who was a trusted advisor to the Romanov family. He was also a controversial figure who was rumored to have supernatural powers. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he was a time traveler.~";
Constant TX_PS_3180 = "~Groucho Marx was an American comedian, actor, and writer who was best known for his work with the Marx Brothers. He was also a successful solo performer and a television host. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he could kill people with his eyebrows.~";
Constant TX_PS_3017 = "~Guidestones? They may have been erected by human hands, but they were inspired by the Black Knight Satellite. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_933 = "~Had a feeling someone might come by looking for help. And here you are.~ Hutz grins, showing a few teeth. ~I'm not going anywhere, not yet. Not until I've done what I need to do.~";
Constant TX_PS_3273 = "~Hard to say. It doesn't look like a very happy place. But then, I don't think laundromats are supposed to be happy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3206 = "~Harris? He's a vampire, as I was telling Margaret just the other day. He played a pivotal role in the election of Ronald Reagan, when he was only seven years old!~";
Constant TX_PS_3189 = "~Harry S Truman was the 33rd President of the United States. He served from 1945 to 1953 and made the decision to drop the atomic bomb on Japan. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that he was a lizard person.~";
Constant TX_PS_2278 = "~Have you ever been inside the Vatican?~";
Constant TX_PS_2172 = "~Have you ever been to Budapest?~";
Constant TX_PS_2173 = "~Have you ever been to Istanbul?~";
Constant TX_PS_2267 = "~Have you ever been to Japan?~";
Constant TX_PS_2255 = "~Have you ever been to Kamchatka?~";
Constant TX_PS_2270 = "~Have you ever heard Tracy Chapman?~";
Constant TX_PS_2256 = "~Have you ever met Mark David Chapman?~";
Constant TX_PS_2959 = "~Have you heard about these new ancient ruins in Kamchatka? Apparently there are some very interesting Koryak artifacts there that suggest a connection to the ancient Sumerians.~";
Constant TX_PS_2155 = "~Have you read this one?~";
Constant TX_PS_2739 = "~He drew Garfield, everyone knows that. He was a really funny guy.~";
Constant TX_PS_2813 = "~He lives in Enigma Lake. He's a doctor. Look for him when you get there.~";
Constant TX_PS_3208 = "~He was a clown who sold hamburgers. And then he became president. I think he was in a movie with a monkey.~";
Constant TX_PS_3233 = "~He was a general who became president. He used to eat Mike and Ike's.~";
Constant TX_PS_3202 = "~He was a kid who suffered from a rare disease that made him think he was a doctor. Mark David Chapman played him on TV.~";
Constant TX_PS_2792 = "~He was a musician. He was a good friend of mine. I warned him about that McCartney guy, but would he listen? No. And look what happened.~";
Constant TX_PS_2807 = "~He was a very funny guy. Never met him. His brothers were very protective, wouldn't let time travelers near him.~";
Constant TX_PS_2788 = "~He was a very good friend of mine. He couldn't stop talking about Edison. I told him to let it go.~";
Constant TX_PS_3199 = "~He was on Saturday Night Live, right?~";
Constant TX_PS_3187 = "~He was on a show, I think. I'd look it up on my phone, but now that we only have flip phones, it's too much trouble.~";
Constant TX_PS_2768 = "~He was some weirdo who named himself after a power company. Freak.~";
Constant TX_PS_3217 = "~He was the guy in the Monkees who lived in a locker.~";
Constant TX_PS_3250 = "~He was the guy in the Monkees who married Yoko Ono, right?~";
Constant TX_PS_3230 = "~He was the guy in the Monkees who wore the hat.~";
Constant TX_PS_3256 = "~He was the guy who came up with the idea for the Monkees, right?~";
Constant TX_PS_2791 = "~He was the leader of the Bolsheviks. There's no truth to the rumor that he was a vampire. I would know.~";
Constant TX_PS_2958 = "~He's a child. That's what you have to understand about Klimp,~ Moira says. ~He's never met a stupid idea he didn't like.~";
Constant TX_PS_2823 = "~He's a field agent. This is his first mission since the unfortunate incident in Budapest.~";
Constant TX_PS_2722 = "~He's a pest, but he's a stupid pest, just like all lizard people. That's what you get for being cold-blooded.~";
Constant TX_PS_345 = "~He's in disguise! Whatever, it doesn't matter. What matters is your mission.~";
Constant TX_PS_2689 = "~He's the field office chief. If you listen real close you can hear the insanity leaking out of his ears.~";
Constant TX_PS_2901 = "~Henry's? Oh, it's a diner. Good coffee. They have a good TV. I used to drink coffee and watch TV,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2454 = "~Hey, Chief, sorry about the --~";
Constant TX_PS_2158 = "~Hi, my name is Larch Faraji.~";
Constant TX_PS_2887 = "~Hmm, I guess I need to flatten those and bring them out back to the dumpster.~";
Constant TX_PS_602 = "~Hmm... take it apart?~";
Constant TX_PS_3058 = "~Hora de la Muerte? It speaks to me. Speaks to me of something ineffable. Something that's not there. Something that's not here. Something that's not anywhere.~";
Constant TX_PS_2943 = "~Horrible woman. Absolutely no appreciation for interactive fiction,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2368 = "~How are you doing, Margaret?~";
Constant TX_PS_2162 = "~How are you doing?~";
Constant TX_PS_2307 = "~How're you doing?~";
Constant TX_PS_2311 = "~How's your mom?~";
Constant TX_PS_3203 = "~Howitzer? He was a genius doctor who believed he was a teenager. But why are we talking about this? Ask me about something important, like Ouija boards.~";
Constant TX_PS_2827 = "~Huffton is a great friend of mine. In some ways, he's the best friend I've ever had. In other ways, he's the worst enemy I've ever had. It's complicated.~";
Constant TX_PS_328 = "~Huh. Thought you would have found it by now. I'm almost certain it's in your Swamp Park office. Go find it and bring it here.~ Doris busies himself at his desk, pointedly ignoring you.";
Constant TX_PS_2688 = "~Hyperspace is a damn pain is what it is.~";
Constant TX_PS_2833 = "~Hyperspace is a four-dimensional plane of being overlaying our own three-dimensional plane. Or something like that. I'm not a physicist.~";
Constant TX_PS_3141 = "~Hypnosis is a state of focused attention and heightened suggestibility that is induced by a hypnotist. It is used in entertainment, therapy, and research. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that it can be used to control people's minds.~";
Constant TX_PS_3026 = "~Hypnosis? I don't know. But I do know that Hipgnosis is a design firm. They did the cover for Dark Side of the Moon. I like that cover. I like the triangle. I like the prism. I like the rainbow.~";
Constant TX_PS_2758 = "~I believe it was in an episode of the original Star Trek. I think it was the one with the Gorn.~";
Constant TX_PS_2784 = "~I can do that. I can levitate. But not when people are watching. I suffer from performance anxiety.~";
Constant TX_PS_1127 = "~I could tell you, but it's best if that came from Doris.~";
Constant TX_PS_2940 = "~I didn't really want to write that one, but the publisher insisted,~ Doctor Helpful replies. ~Still, it sold quite well among left-handed readers.~";
Constant TX_PS_2744 = "~I don't believe in it. I mean, Betty and Barney? That can't be a coincidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_2729 = "~I don't know for sure. I think Klimp might have met one. He's got a lot of stories.~";
Constant TX_PS_2790 = "~I don't know what you're talking about. I've never seen a huge alien jellyfish. I don't know what you're talking about.~";
Constant TX_PS_2748 = "~I don't like to speak ill of the dead. But they should have stayed in the tent.~";
Constant TX_PS_3181 = "~I don't watch horror movies.~";
Constant TX_PS_2886 = "~I doubt you'll be needing any of that now, but if you do, let me know.~";
Constant TX_PS_2925 = "~I got it for a steal at an overstock sale,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_3275 = "~I hope not. I don't like aliens.~";
Constant TX_PS_2861 = "~I know it's a dump. I just work here.~";
Constant TX_PS_2947 = "~I know quite a bit about them, actually. Parser-based games, like this one, allow you to type commands to interact with the world. They're a bit more complex than choice-based games, but they're also more flexible and immersive. I've written a whole slew of books on the subject, you know,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2905 = "~I like Dragnet,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2932 = "~I like it. Good for the constitution,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2897 = "~I like the coffee at Henry's,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2865 = "~I like the ones with the little camels on them. Not to smoke, just to look at.~";
Constant TX_PS_2898 = "~I like to sleep on my side,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2721 = "~I like to think of it as my most productive hobby.~";
Constant TX_PS_2151 = "~I like your desk.~";
Constant TX_PS_3163 = "~I love their song ~Blitzkrieg Bop.~";
Constant TX_PS_2817 = "~I never thought it would go over so big. I was just playing a joke on Charles Dawson. He was so gullible.~";
Constant TX_PS_2801 = "~I once went on a mission back in time to save them from an stealth attack by the Dave Clark Five. They never knew. They never knew.~";
Constant TX_PS_2820 = "~I once went undercover as a Swiss Guard to protect the Pope from a lizard person diguised as a cardinal. In the end I got a commendation and a Swiss Army knife.~";
Constant TX_PS_2731 = "~I remember when that happened. The three of us -- Charlotte, Eleanor, and me -- were having a grand time at Versailles. Then they went off and got lost in time. It was a mess.~";
Constant TX_PS_2165 = "~I see you have a Rubik's cube.~";
Constant TX_PS_2164 = "~I see you have a model TARDIS.~";
Constant TX_PS_2809 = "~I set him up with Eleanor. I thought they'd be good for each other. Boy, was I wrong.~";
Constant TX_PS_2864 = "~I take them by the handful.~";
Constant TX_PS_3246 = "~I think about that thumb drive? It looks like a perfectly ordinary thumb drive. Except for the directions to Atlantis scratched on the side.~";
Constant TX_PS_3267 = "~I think it's a kind of bear. But I'm not sure.~";
Constant TX_PS_3175 = "~I think it's a type of fabric. Like polyester.~";
Constant TX_PS_2891 = "~I think they're from the 70s. I don't know who they are.~";
Constant TX_PS_2806 = "~I tried it once. It didn't work out. I'm not cut out for it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2795 = "~I used to have one of those. I asked it if it worked. It said ~Ask again later.~ I never did get an answer.~";
Constant TX_PS_1118 = "~I was hunting down Savra's minions,~ Daniels says, ~but they caught me and sent me way back to the past. I've been stuck here ever since.~";
Constant TX_PS_2737 = "~I was not involved. I was in the Bahamas at the time. I have witnesses.~";
Constant TX_PS_2811 = "~I was there. I said to Eisenhower, ~You should call it D-Day.~ He thought for a while and then looked at me and said, ~Who are you?~";
Constant TX_PS_2935 = "~I wrote that one during a particularly productive summer. I think it's quite good,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2939 = "~I wrote that one on commission. I don't like to talk about it,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2803 = "~I wrote that song one day sitting in this very office. Once when I was back in 1967 the Monkees heard me humming it. I sold it to them, but they just gave it to the Ramones. I'm still bitter.~";
Constant TX_PS_2835 = "~I'm Christy. I'm the paranormal researcher here. I'm the one they turn to when they need someone's advice to ignore.~";
Constant TX_PS_2679 = "~I'm Maggie. I'm the receptionist here at the BOSH Hyperspace Field Office. I'm here to help you with whatever you need, as long as it's not touching the control panel.~";
Constant TX_PS_2691 = "~I'm Minerva. I'm the field agent here at the BOSH Hyperspace Field Office. I'm the only sane one here.~";
Constant TX_PS_2845 = "~I'm a paranormal illustrator. I draw things that don't exist. It's a very lucrative field.~";
Constant TX_PS_2923 = "~I'm a tweedy old professor with ink-stained fingers,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2847 = "~I'm extremely photosensitive.~";
Constant TX_PS_2956 = "~I'm fine,~ Moira says. ~Why wouldn't I be?~";
Constant TX_PS_2337 = "~I'm going to smack you with a turnip,~ says Faraji.";
Constant TX_PS_2338 = "~I'm going to thwack you with a potato,~ says Faraji.";
Constant TX_PS_2960 = "~I'm great!~ Margaret says. ~So many things to unpack!~";
Constant TX_PS_2962 = "~I'm reading about the latest discoveries in the field of cryptozoology,~ Klimp says. ~Did you know that the Yeti is actually a type of bear? I don't mean a regular bear, but a bear that's not of this world.~";
Constant TX_PS_2892 = "~I'm really trying to make do with what we have.~";
Constant TX_PS_2376 = "~I'm sure you know all about the Chu--~";
Constant TX_PS_2678 = "~I'm surprised you don't know. It's a USB drive. It's used to store data.~";
Constant TX_PS_2818 = "~I'm the one who taught him how to play the tambourine. So much more talented than Mike Nesmith.";
Constant TX_PS_978 = "~I've got a new number, I've got a new line, I've got a new life, and you're not in mine.~";
Constant TX_PS_2727 = "~I've got one in my backyard. Man, I go through a lot of goats.~";
Constant TX_PS_2966 = "~I've heard of people who have been there, even lived there. My friend Doris. True story.~";
Constant TX_PS_2878 = "~I've never been in there. I hear it's a dump.~";
Constant TX_PS_2972 = "~I've often thought that it would be a great subject for a television show. Not a documentary, mind you, but a drama. That guy, you know, from the show about the doctor in the spaceship, he'd be perfect as Sasquatch.~";
Constant TX_PS_3194 = "~II? It was all a misunderstanding. The Germans were building an army of lizard people to conquer the world. The Japanese, who spoke very little German, thought that the lizard people were going to surface in Hawaii. So they attacked Pearl Harbor to stop them. The Americans, who were secretly building a robot army, thought that the Japanese were attacking them. So they joined the war. And Mussolini, of course, was a vampire.~";
Constant TX_PS_2875 = "~If I see an alien, I'm going to ask for a ride.~";
Constant TX_PS_2754 = "~If that's really the image of a man on the shroud, he looks kind of weird. I'm just saying.~";
Constant TX_PS_2882 = "~If you know, you know.~";
Constant TX_PS_3053 = "~Illinois? It's pretty much a dump, except for New York. New York, Illinois is a great place. You should visit their Natural History Museum. They have the best stuff.~";
Constant TX_PS_3004 = "~Illuminati? Of course. They're everywhere. They're in the government, in the media, in the music industry. They're in the Bureau. They're in the BOSH offices. They're in the White House. They're in the Vatican. They're in the Black Knight Satellite.~ Klimp looks around. ~They're in this room... okay, maybe not this room. And hopefully not in the BOSH offices. But they're everywhere else. You don't think Margaret's Illuminati, do you?~";
Constant TX_PS_2993 = "~Incident? It's a mystery. There's not even such a place as the Ural Mountains. It's a cover-up. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_2975 = "~Incident? Time slips are cool. I've seen one. I've been in one. Or was it two? I can't remember.~";
Constant TX_PS_2709 = "~Is that important when the fate of the world is at stake?~";
Constant TX_PS_2314 = "~Is that your cat?~ Faraji asks.";
Constant TX_PS_2378 = "~Is the Yeti --~";
Constant TX_PS_2370 = "~Is time travel --~";
Constant TX_PS_975 = "~Isn't it strange I don't love you? Isn't it strange I don't care? Isn't it strange I don't want you? Isn't it strange I'm not there?~";
Constant TX_PS_2772 = "~Isn't that where Aquaman lives? I think I've been there. It's a nice place.~";
Constant TX_PS_3224 = "~Istanbul is the largest city in Turkey. It is known for its historic sites, its vibrant culture, and its strategic location between Europe and Asia. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that it is a haven for lizard people.~";
Constant TX_PS_3050 = "~It certainly seems a bit fishy to me. It seems too small. I think it's a fake.~";
Constant TX_PS_2913 = "~It is ours,~ hisses the lizard person. ~You will not have it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3272 = "~It looks dirty.~";
Constant TX_PS_3270 = "~It makes me sad to think about it. All those hopeless people pawning their possessions. It's a tragedy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3196 = "~It was a time when everyone was sad. It happened when the Monkees broke up.~";
Constant TX_PS_3211 = "~It was a war in Vietnam. The Monkees were very against it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2684 = "~It was the answer to a question I asked myself. I don't remember the question, but the answer was Budapest.~";
Constant TX_PS_3193 = "~It was the second war in the world. Why do you ask me these things?~";
Constant TX_PS_2814 = "~It wasn't as fun as they make it out to be. Everyone was so serious.~";
Constant TX_PS_2844 = "~It's Doris's little kingdom. It's where we peons toil. I'm not bitter.~";
Constant TX_PS_2713 = "~It's a CMY cube. Light filters through each side in a different color. Alien technology, swear to God.~";
Constant TX_PS_2694 = "~It's a USB drive. It's used to store data. I don't know why you're asking me about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2763 = "~It's a band. They're very good. I've got all their albums. My favorite is ~Istanbul Not Constantinople.~~";
Constant TX_PS_2825 = "~It's a book. It's a very important book. It's the key to the mission. But I'm not sure that's the title. I'm sure you'll figure it out.~";
Constant TX_PS_2753 = "~It's a book. It's a very strange book. I've got a translation around here somewhere.~";
Constant TX_PS_2757 = "~It's a box. A very special box. I've got one in my garage.~";
Constant TX_PS_2696 = "~It's a coffee maker. It makes coffee. It's on my desk.~";
Constant TX_PS_2796 = "~It's a competing agency. They're not as good as we are. They don't have a Doris.~";
Constant TX_PS_2673 = "~It's a control panel. It controls things. You're not allowed to touch it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2944 = "~It's a cozy place, isn't it? I've spent many a happy hour here,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_3081 = "~It's a creature that is said to inhabit Loch Ness in the Scottish Highlands. There have been numerous sightings of the creature, but there is no conclusive evidence that it exists.~";
Constant TX_PS_494 = "~It's a family heirloom. I'd like to get it back.~";
Constant TX_PS_2732 = "~It's a hockey team. I was once a goalie for them. I was terrible.~";
Constant TX_PS_2900 = "~It's a lake,~ Hutz replies. ~Or did you mean the town? I'll miss it. Good little town. Or rather, a crappy little town with a good diner.~";
Constant TX_PS_2716 = "~It's a mystic compass. Hold on to it. It might come in handy. It can find anything, even things that aren't lost.~";
Constant TX_PS_2805 = "~It's a pity the world never got to hear my version of ~Blitzkrieg Bop.~ I think it would have been a hit.~";
Constant TX_PS_2736 = "~It's a place where people go to argue. I don't know why they don't just go to a bar.~";
Constant TX_PS_2828 = "~It's a place where time and space are a little more flexible. It's a good place to keep a field office.~";
Constant TX_PS_3078 = "~It's a plane of existence that exists beyond the physical world. It's a place where spirits and other entities reside. It's not real, of course. But it's a popular subject in the occult.~";
Constant TX_PS_2837 = "~It's a portal that leads to the past. I'm not sure what else you want me to say.~";
Constant TX_PS_2871 = "~It's a real bargain. Um, I mean, it's a real computer. The guy was clear on that. Twelve hundred bucks.~";
Constant TX_PS_3080 = "~It's a region in the western part of the North Atlantic Ocean where a number of aircraft and ships are said to have disappeared under mysterious circumstances.~";
Constant TX_PS_2789 = "~It's a sea. It's a very strange sea. It's full of seaweed. I don't like it. Klimp has some strange ideas about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_3168 = "~It's a song by the Ramones that was released in 1976. It is considered one of the band's signature songs. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that it was written by the Monkees.~";
Constant TX_PS_2778 = "~It's a sports network. I used to be a program director there. I was terrible.~";
Constant TX_PS_2692 = "~It's a temporal paradox waiting to happen. Why anyone would put Doris in charge of it is beyond me.~";
Constant TX_PS_3077 = "~It's a theoretical concept that involves moving between different points in time. It's not possible, of course. But it's a popular subject in science fiction.~";
Constant TX_PS_2783 = "~It's a way of making people do what you want. I'm very good at it. I can make people do anything. Anything.~";
Constant TX_PS_2769 = "~It's a way of predicting the future. It's a very accurate science. I'm a Leo, by the way.~";
Constant TX_PS_2730 = "~It's a way of selling bad art to people who don't know any better. But it's also a way of understanding the universe. It's a mixed bag.~";
Constant TX_PS_3166 = "~It's by the Monkees. I think it's about the Vietnam War.~";
Constant TX_PS_2755 = "~It's hard to say. I thought I had it once, but it turned out to be a coffee cup.~";
Constant TX_PS_2826 = "~It's here, and yet it's not here. But, no, actually, it is here. It's a very confusing concept.~";
Constant TX_PS_2829 = "~It's how we get around. It's a very useful thing. Dreadfully expensive to maintain, though.~";
Constant TX_PS_2907 = "~It's loud. I like loud,~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2890 = "~It's not much, but it's better than the floor.~";
Constant TX_PS_2888 = "~It's not much, but what can you expect for $8?~";
Constant TX_PS_2931 = "~It's not really ink. It's elderberry juice,~ Doctor Helpful replies.";
Constant TX_PS_3069 = "~It's okay, Larch. I'm sure whoever's calling will give up eventually.~";
Constant TX_PS_2830 = "~It's our backup. Not as flexible as the main portal, but it gets the job done.~";
Constant TX_PS_2759 = "~It's the original science. It's the philosophy of understanding the essence of things. It's a very profitable hobby.~";
Constant TX_PS_3236 = "~It's where Budapest is, right?~";
Constant TX_PS_3239 = "~It's where the Monkees are from.~";
Constant TX_PS_2723 = "~It's where we are right now. It's a place where time and space are a little more flexible. It's a good place to keep a field office.~";
Constant TX_PS_3192 = "~Japan is an island nation in East Asia. It is known for its rich cultural heritage, its technological innovations, and its cuisine. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that they built a giant robot to take over the world.~";
Constant TX_PS_3191 = "~Japan? They attacked Pearl Harbor to cover up the fact that they were building a giant robot. They were going to use it to take over the world. But they couldn't get it to work. So they built a giant lizard instead.~";
Constant TX_PS_2767 = "~Jeez, I don't know everything. Let's talk about something else.~";
Constant TX_PS_3096 = "~Jefferson Davis was the President of the Confederate States of America during the American Civil War. He never said anything about the Black Knight Satellite.~";
Constant TX_PS_2984 = "~Jefferson Davis? Most people just know him as the guy who first posited the existence of the Black Knight Satellite. But he was also President of the Confederacy, did you know that?~";
Constant TX_PS_3151 = "~John Lennon is an English singer, songwriter, and peace activist who co-founded the Beatles, the most commercially successful band in the history of popular music. Klimp is right about this one -- he's still alive and living inside the Earth.~";
Constant TX_PS_2431 = "~John Lennon's --~";
Constant TX_PS_3218 = "~Jones? He was a pirate. And a vampire. And a member of the Monkees. But most people don't know that he was also a time traveler. Despite the rumors, I never met him in Budapest.~";
Constant TX_PS_987 = "~Just because you're not so bright, doesn't mean you're not alright, and I'd never call you a moron.~";
Constant TX_PS_2867 = "~Just watch your step.~";
Constant TX_PS_342 = "~Just what it sounds like. It's a bipedal, intelligent reptilian creature. Strange people. Deathly allergic to rutabagas.~";
Constant TX_PS_3222 = "~Kamchatka is a peninsula in the Russian Far East. It is known for its volcanoes, geysers, and hot springs. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that it has any connection to ancient Sumeria.~";
Constant TX_PS_3054 = "~Kamchatka? It's a peninsula in far eastern Russia. It was once the leading contender for most uninteresting location on Earth. But then they found those ruins. Now it's the leading contender for most interesting location on Earth.~";
Constant TX_PS_2982 = "~Kelly-Hopkinsville Encounter? It's just silly. Everyone knows that part of Kentucky is riddled with alien activity. I mean, Jefferson Davis was from there, wasn't he?~";
Constant TX_PS_3095 = "~Kentucky is a state in the southeastern United States. It is known for its horse racing, bourbon, and bluegrass music. It is also known for the Kelly-Hopkinsville Encounter. There is no truth to anything Klimp says about it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2983 = "~Kentucky? Most suspicious state in the Union, after Montana. I wouldn't trust anyone from there. Not even Colonel Sanders.~";
Constant TX_PS_2919 = "~Klimp is a good fr-- um, I mean enemy of the lizard people,~ hisses the tall lizard person.";
Constant TX_PS_3014 = "~Knights Templar? Consider this -- they're not Knights at all. They're really kind of fun, you know. They're like the Freemasons, but with swords. And they have the Spear of Destiny. Or they did. Or they didn't. I can't remember.~";
Constant TX_PS_3271 = "~Laundromat? I don't know. I don't do my own laundry. I have a guy for that.~";
Constant TX_PS_3035 = "~Lennon? Imagine he's still alive. I've seen the evidence. Mark David Chapman didn't kill him. He's living in a hidden city on the inside of the earth. But I don't think that's what you meant. You meant Lenin, didn't you? I can't remember what I think about him.~";
Constant TX_PS_1109 = "~Let me see, now.~ Daniels theatrically searches his ragged suit. ~Nope. No screwdriver.~";
Constant TX_PS_3142 = "~Levitation is the act of rising or hovering in the air without any physical support. It is a popular subject in magic, religion, and popular culture. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of levitation.~";
Constant TX_PS_3123 = "~Ley lines are hypothetical alignments of ancient sites, such as stone circles, megaliths, and churches. They are said to have spiritual significance and to carry mystical energy. There is no scientific evidence to support the claims of ley lines.~";
Constant TX_PS_3124 = "~Leyden jars are early devices that were used to store static electricity. They were invented in the 18th century by Pieter van Musschenbroek and Ewald Georg von Kleist. I'm not sure why you're asking me about them.~";
Constant TX_PS_3034 = "~Lights? Don't let anyone know, but they're really just the headlights of a car. A car from another world. I've seen the evidence.~";
Constant TX_PS_2988 = "~Lights? No one knows what they were. Not even me. But I have a theory. It's a theory that involves a bear from another world. At least, I think it does.~";
Constant TX_PS_2766 = "~Listen, it's like a big connect-the-dots book, except the dots are places and the lines are energy. It's a very simple concept.~";
Constant TX_PS_2903 = "~Lizard people? What are you talking about?~ Hutz replies.";
Constant TX_PS_2969 = "~Loch Ness Monster? Of course. I've seen it. It's a plesiosaur, you know. From another world.~";
Constant TX_PS_2810 = "~Long time ago, middle Edo period. I was an early proponent of kabuki theater. I had to quit because of my allergy to face paint.~";
Constant TX_PS_3953 = "~Love~ means 0 in tennis.";
Constant TX_PS_3043 = "~Made it myself. Well, not really built it, but I bought it. It's the kind of desk you could imagine Tesla using. I just read an article about him. They completely left out the part about him meeting the Jersey Devil.~";
Constant TX_PS_2706 = "~Maggie is our receptionist. She can help you with anything you need.~";
Constant TX_PS_2840 = "~Maggie is... Maggie. She's the receptionist. She's very good at her job -- it's just that no one knows what that is. I'm not being sarcastic.~";
Constant TX_PS_3155 = "~Magic 8-Balls are toys that are used for fortune-telling or seeking advice. They are shaped like an eight-ball and contain a 20-sided die with various answers. There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that they can predict the future.~";
Constant TX_PS_2698 = "~Make sure your hands are clean before you touch the books.~";
Constant TX_PS_2998 = "~Manuscript? It's a hoax. I've seen the evidence. It's a hoax. But it's a good hoax. I like it.~";
Constant TX_PS_2623 = "~Margaret, do we have any money in petty cash?~";
Constant TX_PS_2654 = "~Margaret, do you think there's going to be an alien invasion?~";
Constant TX_PS_2564 = "~Margaret, have you ever seen a movie by the Marx Brothers?~";
Constant TX_PS_2642 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Anastasia?~";
Constant TX_PS_2458 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Budapest?~";
Constant TX_PS_2599 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Davy Jones?~";
Constant TX_PS_2584 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Doogie Howser?~";
Constant TX_PS_2614 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Dwight Eisenhower?~";
Constant TX_PS_2567 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Franklin Delano Roosevelt?~";
Constant TX_PS_2561 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Groucho Marx?~";
Constant TX_PS_2570 = "~Margaret, what do you know about Harry S Truman?~";
