Constant TX_PS_1205 = "Actually it smells better than Swamp Park.";
Constant TX_PS_3604 = "Ad";
Constant TX_PS_146 = "Adjacent light";
Constant TX_PS_220 = "Advanced Temporal Mechanics";
Constant TX_PS_699 = "Afraid of lizard people? With good reason! Chip Flemki reveals how many there are, where they live, and what coffee shops they frequent. Not for the faint of heart.";
Constant TX_PS_390 = "Agent Faraji is dressed smartly in a black suit, with neat hair and a serious expression. They are every bit the professional.";
Constant TX_PS_1247 = "Agent Gaunt's last name describes him well. He is a perpetually worried-looking individual, a look emphasized by his thinness and his thick-rimmed glasses.";
Constant TX_PS_1249 = "Agent Goldberg has lots of dogs, a fact which can be inferred by the inevitable fur somewhere on her person. The last front office worker at the Bureau left due to an extreme allergic reaction to Goldberg.";
Constant TX_PS_609 = "Agent Moira Zin is the very model of a competent Bureau agent. Hard-working, serious, no-nonsense but open-minded, she's the sober counter-balance to Klimp's sometimes childish credulity. Moira would clearly be a rising star if it weren't for the Bureau's pending dissolution.";
Constant TX_PS_3997 = "Ah, a key to a gym locker. Faraji better take it.";
Constant TX_PS_2042 = "Ah, the stink of the dumpster. Faraji leaves the astral tunnel for the back lot.";
Constant TX_PS_3434 = "Alchemy is an ancient branch of natural philosophy, a philosophical and protoscientific tradition practiced throughout Europe, Africa, and Asia, originating in Greco-Roman Egypt in the first few centuries AD. It aims to purify, mature, and perfect certain objects. Modern thinking has dismissed alchemy as a pseudoscience, but it has had a significant influence on the development of modern science, particularly chemistry.";
Constant TX_PS_1469 = "Alchemy";
Constant TX_PS_1734 = "Alien invasion";
Constant TX_PS_3458 = "Aliens are extraterrestrial beings that have visited Earth. They are often said to be the cause of unexplained phenomena, such as UFO sightings, crop circles, and cattle mutilations. The existence of aliens is disputed by the scientific community, but has been proven by numerous eyewitness accounts and photographs.";
Constant TX_PS_1495 = "Aliens";
Constant TX_PS_3503 = "All immobile.";
Array TX_L_3503 --> CONSTANT_PACKED_TEXT_STORAGE TX_PS_3503;
Constant TX_PS_708 = "Ambush and Alliteration";
Constant TX_PS_3427 = "Amelia Earhart was an American aviation pioneer and author. Earhart was the first woman to fly solo across the Atlantic Ocean. She received the U.S. Distinguished Flying Cross for this record. She set many other records, wrote best-selling books about her flying experiences, and was instrumental in the formation of The Ninety-Nines, an organization of female pilots. She was also a member of the National Women's Party, and an early supporter of the Equal Rights Amendment. She disappeared mysteriously in 1937 while attempting to circumnavigate the globe. Many theories have been proposed about her disappearance, but none have been proven.";
Constant TX_PS_1462 = "Amelia Earhart";
Constant TX_PS_612 = "An Inscrutable Enigma";
Constant TX_PS_3 = "An Interactive Phenomenon";
Constant TX_PS_249 = "An acrylic cube that filters light on different wavelengths through its various sides.";
Constant TX_PS_1190 = "An almost imperceptible breeze wafts through the basement, smelling faintly of sewage.";
Constant TX_PS_4206 = "An attack is usually coming when the lizard people pick up a root vegetable.";
Constant TX_PS_1917 = "An automatic car wash isn't of much use when one is on foot.";
Constant TX_PS_506 = "An everyday blue dumpster, about six feet high.";
Constant TX_PS_1056 = "An intricate tapestry, depicting a scene of a medieval village. It's a bit out of place in a church, but it's lovely.";
Constant TX_PS_1890 = "An old, creaky wood floor.";
Constant TX_PS_1216 = "An old-fashioned swinging door, it reads ~Henry's Hot Skillet~.";
Constant TX_PS_504 = "An ordinary chain link fence, about eight feet high.";
Constant TX_PS_1183 = "An ordinary door.";
Constant TX_PS_839 = "An ordinary sales counter.";
Constant TX_PS_1564 = "An unremarkable white metal door leads into the BOSH offices.";
Constant TX_PS_1726 = "Anastasia Romanov";
Constant TX_PS_1632 = "Anatomy of a Hoax: Writings on Modern Medicine's Greatest Myths";
Constant TX_PS_1482 = "Ancient Egypt";
Constant TX_PS_3445 = "Ancient astronauts is the idea that intelligent extraterrestrial beings visited Earth and made contact with humans in antiquity and prehistoric times. Proponents suggest that this contact influenced the development of human cultures, technologies, and religions. The idea has been popularized by authors such as Erich von Däniken, who wrote the 1968 book Chariots of the Gods?, and has been the subject of numerous books, documentaries, and films.";
Constant TX_PS_1481 = "Ancient astronauts";
Constant TX_PS_3572 = "And Gob begat Bob, and Bob begat Rob, and Rob begat Job, and Job begat Chauncey, and Chauncey begat Hank, and all told there were fifty-two generations between Gob and Gob XII, who was the last of the line. And Gob XII begat no one, for he was a eunuch. And the Lord said, ~That's what you get for hanging out with lizard people.~";
Constant TX_PS_3569 = "And God so loved the world that he gave his only begotten son, that whosoever believeth in him should not perish, but have everlasting life. The lizard people are not included in this offer.";
Constant TX_PS_3500 = "And behold the Lord created the rutabaga, and the lizard people tasted of it and were repulsed, and the Lord said, ~I shall smite thee with the rutabaga,~ and the lizard people said, ~No, not the rutabaga!~";
Array TX_L_3500 --> CONSTANT_PACKED_TEXT_STORAGE TX_PS_3500;
Constant TX_PS_1995 = "And deprive the laundromat of its livelihood?";
Constant TX_PS_3584 = "And in the town of Gabblehouse was born an infant to a woman named Gorma, and the Lord said, ~That's a terrible name.~";
Constant TX_PS_3570 = "And it came to be that the Lord made aliens, and he saw that they were good, and he made lizard people, and he saw that they were not good. And he made humans, and he saw that they were not good either. And he made the platypus, and he saw that it was good. But later the humans became good, sort of like Godzilla.";
Constant TX_PS_3583 = "And lo, the lizard people rebelled against the Lord, and the Lord said, ~I'm not going to put up with that.~";
Constant TX_PS_2012 = "And put them where? They're fine where they are.";
Constant TX_PS_1980 = "And rob the community of one of its few sources of culture?";
Constant TX_PS_3575 = "And the Lord said, ~I am the Lord, and I am a jealous God, and I will visit the iniquity of the fathers upon the children unto the third and fourth generation of them that hate me, and show mercy unto thousands of them that love me and keep my commandments.~ And the lizard people said, ~We hate you.~";
Constant TX_PS_3585 = "And the Lord said, ~I shall rain down upon thee with great vengeance and furious anger,~ and the lizard people said, ~We've heard that before.~";
Constant TX_PS_3571 = "And the Lord said, ~Let there be light,~ and there was light. And the Lord said, ~Let there be lizard people,~ and there were lizard people. And the Lord said, ~Let there be humans,~ and there were humans. And the Lord said, ~Let there be platypuses,~ and there were platypuses.";
Constant TX_PS_3566 = "And the Lord said, ~The path of the righteous is beset on all sides by the inequities of the selfish and the tyranny of the lizard people. Blessed is he who smites the lizard people, even if only with a rutabaga.";
Constant TX_PS_3582 = "And the Lord was attending his weekly reading circle, when he had an idea. ~I shall make a world,~ he said, ~and I shall call it Earth.~ And the lizard people said, ~That's a terrible name.~";
Constant TX_PS_3574 = "And the hosts of the lizard people came down from the mountains, and they were many, and they were fierce, and they were hungry. And the Lord said, ~I'm not going to feed them, they're your problem.~";
Constant TX_PS_3580 = "And the land was filled with the iniquities of the lizard people, and the Lord said, ~I'm not going to clean that up.~";
Constant TX_PS_4007 = "And then turning it off again?";
Constant TX_PS_4086 = "And what's the significance of the shiny object they're carrying?";
Constant TX_PS_653 = "Andrea D'Andrea";
Constant TX_PS_613 = "André d'Enfer";
Constant TX_PS_713 = "Andy Richter";
Constant TX_PS_463 = "Angel's Department Store";
Constant TX_PS_4083 = "Annoying, aren't they?";
Constant TX_PS_684 = "Anonymous";
Constant TX_PS_57 = "Answers";
Constant TX_PS_623 = "Antonia's life is a mystery to everyone, including herself, and Biff is determined to solve it. But as he starts to learn what lies beneath her enigmatic exterior, he begins to question his own reality. Who is Antonia, and is there even such a person as Biff?";
Constant TX_PS_4071 = "Any ideas?";
Constant TX_PS_656 = "Anywhere But Wherever You Are";
Constant TX_PS_1827 = "Apart from the many wall-coverings, the walls are made of the same white stuff as the rest of hyperspace.";
Constant TX_PS_3536 = "Apparently Margaret has a key for the back door.";
Array TX_L_3536 --> CONSTANT_PACKED_TEXT_STORAGE TX_PS_3536;
Constant TX_PS_1874 = "Apparently stricken with a stunning lack of imagination, someone has installed grey industrial carpet.";
Constant TX_PS_400 = "Apparently the bureau did make off with at least one piece of government furniture. A bland, institutional piece with fake leather seats, it's at least preferable to second-hand upholstery.";
Constant TX_PS_1636 = "Applied Speculation";
Constant TX_PS_3974 = "Are there any books you've seen with similar names?";
Constant TX_PS_2015 = "Are you just trying to tick Margaret off?";
