Constant TX_PS_1960 = "How? Just rip it out of the dashboard?";
Constant TX_PS_3576 = "However, the Lord said to the lizard people, ~I am the Lord of the humans, and I -- oh, and the aliens -- and I will smite you with great vengeance and furious anger and the like.~";
Constant TX_PS_320 = "Huffton Klimp, or simply ~The Chief~, who by his name and title should rightly be big and gruff, is a wiry guy with a thinning shock of red hair on top. Once the youngest and most devoted recruit in the Bureau, the years and his promotion to Bureau Head have not dulled his enthusiasm and idealism. He's a true believer in the existence of aliens, and he's convinced that the Bureau is the only thing standing between humanity and the alien menace. He's also convinced that the Bureau is the only thing standing between him and a comfortable retirement. He's a good guy, but he's a bit of a pain.";
Constant TX_PS_1511 = "Huge alien jellyfish";
Constant TX_PS_4168 = "Hutz has suddenly become unhelpful.";
Constant TX_PS_1972 = "Hutz is using it.";
Constant TX_PS_139 = "Hutz needs hot coffee.";
Constant TX_PS_4177 = "Hutz will apparently only drink really hot coffee.";
Constant TX_PS_920 = "Hutz";
Constant TX_PS_140 = "Hutz-needs-hot-coffee";
Constant TX_PS_145 = "Hyperlight";
Constant TX_PS_149 = "Hyperspace";
Constant TX_PS_3453 = "Hypnosis is a state of human consciousness involving focused attention and reduced peripheral awareness and an enhanced capacity to respond to suggestion. The term may also refer to an art, skill, or act of inducing hypnosis. Theories explaining what occurs during hypnosis fall into two groups. Altered state theories see hypnosis as an altered state of mind or trance, marked by a level of awareness different from the ordinary state of consciousness. In contrast, nonstate theories see hypnosis as a form of imaginative role enactment. During hypnosis, a person is said to have heightened focus and concentration. The person can concentrate intensely on a specific thought or memory, while blocking out sources of distraction. Hypnotized subjects are said to show an increased response to suggestions.";
Constant TX_PS_1489 = "Hypnosis";
Constant TX_PS_416 = "Hyundai hood";
Constant TX_PS_273 = "I believe that kind of art is called abstract astigmatism.";
Constant TX_PS_187 = "I bet they don't get much foot traffic here.";
Constant TX_PS_1967 = "I can see the headlines now: ~Local agent arrested for stealing a laundromat.~";
Constant TX_PS_3935 = "I don't suppose singing to it will help.";
Constant TX_PS_3934 = "I guess we're hoping the glow will do something interesting.";
Constant TX_PS_3534 = "I wonder if any of this stuff is important.";
