Constant TX_PS_4117 = "Lenses are used to focus light.";
Constant TX_PS_3455 = "Levitation is the process by which a mystic rises into the air, or floats in the air, without any physical support, and in a way that defies the laws of gravity. In addition, many UFOs are said to be capable of levitation.";
Constant TX_PS_1491 = "Levitation";
Constant TX_PS_3440 = "Ley lines are alleged alignments of a number of places of geographical and historical interest, such as ancient monuments and megaliths, natural ridge-tops and water-fords. Their existence was suggested in 1921 by the amateur archaeologist Alfred Watkins, in his book The Old Straight Track. The ancient surveyors who supposedly made the lines were given the name ~dodmen~. Watkins believed that the lines were created for ease of overland navigation, and that the ancient surveyors used the lines as a guide across the landscape. He suggested that the lines could have been created by prehistoric peoples, and that they were used for navigation, trade, and ceremonial purposes. Watkins~ ideas were later expanded upon by other researchers, and the concept of ley lines has become popular in the New Age movement and in esoteric and occult circles. Ley lines are often said to be sources of mystical energy, and are often associated with other paranormal phenomena, such as UFO sightings and crop circles.";
Constant TX_PS_1475 = "Ley lines";
Constant TX_PS_1476 = "Leyden jars";
Constant TX_PS_467 = "Li'l Nectarine Convenience Store";
Constant TX_PS_486 = "Li'l Nectarine Gift Card";
Constant TX_PS_550 = "Li'l Nectarine offers great service and low prices, or so they say. This one's cluttered aisles and sparse shelves could make one wonder if that's true. Behind the counter is the typical array of cigarettes and lottery tickets. Under the counter is a glass case containing various useful items.";
Constant TX_PS_1736 = "Liberace";
Constant TX_PS_76 = "Life is hard.";
Constant TX_PS_4220 = "Like a screwdriver, maybe.";
Constant TX_PS_1881 = "Like everything else astral, the floor (ground?) is a featureless white.";
Constant TX_PS_1897 = "Like everything else here (except the terrible carpet), the ceiling is a featureless white.";
Constant TX_PS_1899 = "Like everything else here, the ceiling is a featureless white.";
Constant TX_PS_1873 = "Like everything else here, the floor (ground?) is a featureless white.";
Constant TX_PS_1902 = "Like the walls, the ceiling is made of corrugated metal.";
Constant TX_PS_688 = "Linus Anagram";
Constant TX_PS_651 = "Lionel Sexton is a poet and a potter. While many might think that just maybe you could combine the two, no one but Sexton has dared to combine them with an historical treatise on the QWERTY keyboard. A runner-up for the Iowa State Fair Poetry Prize, and winner of the Iowa State Fair Pottery Prize.";
Constant TX_PS_649 = "Lionel Sexton";
Constant TX_PS_696 = "Lizard People: The Truth";
Constant TX_PS_1850 = "Loamy dirt walls.";
Constant TX_PS_205 = "Lobby";
Constant TX_PS_1443 = "Loch Ness Monster";
Constant TX_PS_1566 = "Locking-back-door";
Constant TX_PS_4161 = "Look around carefully.";
Constant TX_PS_4111 = "Look around the town for a light source.";
Constant TX_PS_3387 = "Looking tired, Margaret says, ~Chief Klimp needs to get me an assistant. I can't do this all by myself.~";
Constant TX_PS_1612 = "Looks like it was taken out of an old library somewhere.";
Constant TX_PS_559 = "Looks like it's been dropped a few times. And then run over by a truck.";
Constant TX_PS_1101 = "Looks like the vegetables are well-preserved.";
Constant TX_PS_1793 = "Lost cat";
Constant TX_PS_711 = "Lost for centuries, Jane Austen's final novel has finally been discovered. A tale of love, loss, and word play in the Old West, Ambush and Alliteration is a must-read for fans of Austen and anachronisms.";
Constant TX_PS_440 = "Ls-light";
Constant TX_PS_621 = "M. Franke";
Constant TX_PS_3338 = "Maggie curls her lip. ~I don't like coffee. It's too bitter. But Minerva likes it. She's the only one who does. Except for Doris and Christy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3340 = "Maggie gets up for a moment and paces. ~Most people think my job is easy. But it's not. I have so many scary thoughts sitting here all day.~";
Constant TX_PS_195 = "Maggie is sitting at the desk, doing nothing Faraji can discern.";
Constant TX_PS_3337 = "Maggie looks at her hands. ~Once I thought I wasn't real. But Minerva told me I was. So I guess I am.~";
Constant TX_PS_3335 = "Maggie looks up from her desk. ~Do you know what makes this place so special? It's the people. I mean, not the people that you see, but the others.~";
Constant TX_PS_2674 = "Maggie looks up without seeming to focus on anything in particular. ~It's the place that isn't quite is. It's where we are now. It's where we go when we leave here.~";
Constant TX_PS_3334 = "Maggie seems to snap out of her reverie. ~Oh, hello. Who are you again? Oh yes, Agent Faraji. Please don't touch the control panel.~";
Constant TX_PS_3336 = "Maggie snaps her fingers. ~That's it! I remember now. Budapest.~";
Constant TX_PS_362 = "Maggie snaps out of her reverie. ~Oh, you're ready to go? I'll activate the auxiliary portal for you~ She types rapidly on her control panel, then says ~It's all ready -- go west down the hallway and turn to the back into Portal Room 2.~";
Constant TX_PS_3339 = "Maggie twirls a lock of hair around her finger. ~A lot of people travel in time and don't even know it. They think they're just going to the store or to work. But they're not. They're going to the past or the future.~";
Constant TX_PS_194 = "Maggie";
Constant TX_PS_1505 = "Magic 8-Ball";
Constant TX_PS_765 = "Main Street runs east from here, while Solvay Road heads north. South of here, Henry's Hot Skillet promises all of the comforts of the mid-twentieth-century diner. A bookstore named The Reading Room lies to the west, while Fresnel's Music is southwest.";
Constant TX_PS_795 = "Main and Lake";
Constant TX_PS_764 = "Main and Solvay";
Constant TX_PS_796 = "Main goes west, while Lake runs north. The corner of the town hall is to the northwest, although it cannot be entered there. Southeast is the entrance to WGXC ~Galaxy~ Radio. There is a broadcast tower on top of the building.";
Constant TX_PS_3982 = "Make some noise.";
Constant TX_PS_1781 = "Mao Zedong";
Constant TX_PS_1755 = "Maple syrup";
Constant TX_PS_1842 = "Marble at the base, then white plaster.";
Constant TX_PS_1500 = "Marfa Lights";
Constant TX_PS_392 = "Margaret Chao";
Constant TX_PS_3386 = "Margaret brushes a lock of hair out of her face. ~I'm going to have to get a haircut soon. I can't see anything.~";
Constant TX_PS_106 = "Margaret does not have a screwdriver.";
Constant TX_PS_3395 = "Margaret grimaces. ~I went over to look at the pawn shop, and the guy tried to hit on me. I told him I was married, but he didn't care. Do you think I'm bad for lying?~";
Constant TX_PS_109 = "Margaret has the key to the back door.";
Constant TX_PS_2009 = "Margaret has very carefully arranged the room, as much as it looks like chaos.";
Constant TX_PS_3553 = "Margaret is a bit flaky, but usually helpful. Her home base is the front office, but she periodically wanders off to throw things away in the dumpster out back.";
Array TX_L_3553 --> CONSTANT_PACKED_TEXT_STORAGE TX_PS_3553;
Constant TX_PS_2014 = "Margaret likes it where it is.";
Constant TX_PS_2957 = "Margaret looks around and then whispers, ~I don't think he likes me.~";
Constant TX_PS_3389 = "Margaret looks around, then whispers, ~I don't think the Chief likes me. He's always so grumpy.~";
Constant TX_PS_3388 = "Margaret looks at Faraji and says, ~I don't know how you can stand to wear that suit all day. It looks so hot.~";
Constant TX_PS_3396 = "Margaret looks at her phone. ~I can't believe they're taking away our smart phones. I don't know how I'm going to keep in touch with my friends.~";
Constant TX_PS_3397 = "Margaret looks at the coffee table. ~I can't believe they charged us $8 for that. It's not even real wood.~";
Constant TX_PS_3390 = "Margaret looks dismayed. ~I can't believe I forgot to bring my lunch today. I'm going to be starving.~";
Constant TX_PS_3398 = "Margaret looks dreamy. ~Some day I want to go to Budapest, or Istanbul. They both sound so exotic.~";
Constant TX_PS_3542 = "Margaret mentioned that the hex wrench fell into the heating vent behind her desk.";
Array TX_L_3542 --> CONSTANT_PACKED_TEXT_STORAGE TX_PS_3542;
Constant TX_PS_3391 = "Margaret mutters to herself, ~So much to do, so little time.~";
Constant TX_PS_3393 = "Margaret pauses to look at the photos on the wall. ~Everyone looks so happy. I wonder what they're doing now. Well, except you, Moira, and the Chief. I know what you're doing now.~";
Constant TX_PS_3394 = "Margaret pulls a box of staples out of a box. ~I don't know why we have so many staples. We never use them.~";
Constant TX_PS_3385 = "Margaret says thoughtfully, ~I really should organize the office supplies. But I don't have time right now. Soon, I swear.~";
Constant TX_PS_412 = "Margaret";
Constant TX_PS_1940 = "Margaret's put a lot of work into that, don't just take it away from her.";
Constant TX_PS_110 = "Margaret-backdoor-key";
Constant TX_PS_107 = "Margaret-no-screwdriver";
Constant TX_PS_637 = "Marjorie Asphodel";
Constant TX_PS_639 = "Marjorie Asphodel's biting satire of the vampire romance genre is a must-read for anyone who's ever rolled their eyes at a sparkly vampire. Follow the adventures of Ubik and Taylor as they navigate the treacherous waters of high school, love, and the undead. A hilarious romp that will leave you laughing, crying, and possibly vomiting.";
